            "type": "markdown",
            "content": {
              "instructions": [
                "To embed a returns reason capture form in Shopify, follow these steps:",
                "1. Log in to your Shopify admin panel and navigate to the 'Online Store' section.",
                "2. Click on 'Themes' and then select the 'Actions' dropdown menu next to your current theme.",
                "3. Click on 'Edit code' and navigate to the 'templates' folder.",
                "4. Create a new file called 'returns.liquid' and add the following code to capture the returns reason:",
                "<form id='returns-reason-form'>",
                "  <label for='returns-reason'>Reason for Return:</label>",
                "  <textarea id='returns-reason' name='returns-reason'></textarea>",
                "  <button type='submit'>Submit</button>",
                "</form>",
                "5. Add a new script tag to your theme's 'layout.liquid' file to handle the form submission:",
                "<script>",
                "  $(document).ready(function(){",
                "    $('#returns-reason-form').submit(function(event){",
                "      event.preventDefault();",
                "      var reason = $('#returns-reason').val();",
                "      // Send the reason to your server-side logic for processing",
                "    });",
                "  });",
                "</script>",
                "6. In your Shopify theme's settings, add a new metafield to store the captured returns reason:",
                "Go to 'Settings' > 'Themes' > 'Edit code' > 'config.liquid' and add the following code:",
                "metafield: { name: 'returns_reason', description: 'Reason for return' }",
                "7. In your Shopify theme's liquid templates, use the metafield to display the captured returns reason:",
                "Use the following code to display the captured returns reason in your order status page:",
                "{{ order.metafields.returns_reason.value }}",
                "8. Test the returns reason capture form by submitting it and verifying that the reason is stored in the metafield and displayed on the order status page."
              ]
            },
